[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis x line=bottom, axis y line=left, xlabel={Workers $n$}, ylabel={Time $t$ (days)}, xmin=0, xmax=12, ymin=0, ymax=40, domain=2.3:12, samples=100, restrict y to domain=0:40, unbounded coords=jump]
\addplot[thick,blue] {90/x};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*, red] coordinates {(5,18)};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:5,18) {$(5,18)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The graph shows the time $t$ (days) taken to complete a job against the number of workers $n$.
The time $t$ varies inversely with the number of workers $n$.
Use the labelled point to find the equation for $t$ in terms of $n$.
